{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require the publication of value-for-money assessments for asylum accommodation",
        "additional_details": "We support a fair distribution of asylum accommodation across the country. An area\u2019s affluence should neither exclude it nor justify spending more taxpayer money.\r\n \r\nAssessments should compare whole-life costs, including acquisition, adaptation, security, transport and impact on local services. Safety, suitability and residents\u2019 welfare should remain essential.\r\n \r\nWhere a costlier option is selected, the Government should publish its reasons. Fair distribution and responsible spending should go together.",
        "background": "Require the Home Office to publish standardised, value-for-money assessments before approving new asylum accommodation. This should compare all suitable options and explain any possible decision to not select the option offering taxpayers the best overall value.",
